  <header class="flow">
    <h1>Best pollen allergy apps for iPhone</h1>
    <p>We make one of these, so read this with that in mind. What follows is not a ranking with Respira at the top: it is what each app is genuinely best at, taken from their own App Store listings on {{ competitors.snapshotDate }}, including the places where the others are the better answer.</p>
  </header>

  <section class="section flow" aria-labelledby="short-answer">
    <h2 id="short-answer">The short answer</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Longest US track record:</strong> Allergy Plus by Pollen.com. Two decades of US allergy forecasting behind it and around 22,900 ratings. Its listing states it is for the continental US only.</li>
      <li><strong>Predicting how you will feel:</strong> ZYRTEC AllergyCast. It turns your logged symptoms into a personalised daily severity prediction, which none of the others here do.</li>
      <li><strong>Air quality:</strong> IQAir AirVisual, and not close. Over 500,000 locations in 100+ countries, historical data and 3D maps. Pollen is not its focus.</li>
      <li><strong>Pollen outside the US, and a diary you can hand to a doctor:</strong> Respira. Eight countries, eleven US species, an exportable symptom diary, and Home and Lock Screen widgets. It is also the newest here, with no US ratings yet.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

